on":null,"draft":false,"pull_request":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/pulls/117161","html_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117161","diff_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117161.diff","patch_url":"https://github.com/godotengine/godot/pull/117161.patch","merged_at":null},"body":"<!--\r\nPlease target the `master` branch. We will take care of backporting relevant fixes to older versions.\r\n\r\nBefore submitting, please read our checklist for new contributors:\r\nhttps://contributing.godotengine.org/en/latest/engine/introduction.html#checklist-for-new-contributors\r\n-->\r\nFixes : #117150 \r\n\r\nIssue :\r\nNodes with \"Skip Import\" on are being deleted in _post_fix_node. But animation tracks are being created before _post_fix_node, which means we also create tracks for \"Skip Import\" nodes. So we end up with tracks that points to nodes that no longer exist. Creating an error in _post_fix_animations when we try to use get_node using the track's path, we also ended up with theses useless tracks in tracks_to_keep.\r\n\r\nFix :\r\nWe use get_node_or_null instead and delete the tracks that point to deleted nodes\r\n\r\nNote :\r\nI felt that deleting theses tracks in _post_fix_animations made the most sense, but deleting them in _post_fix_node right before deleting the node is also an option","closed_by":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117161/reactions","total_count":4,"+1":4,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":0},"timeline_url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/117161/timeline","performed_via_github_app":null,"state_reason":null}